{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions","id":624000,"title":"Examples of Devotions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-12T02:22:27-07:00","id":624000,"title":"Examples of Devotions","content":"Hi all,<br /> I tried to develop new devotions fallowing the tips given in another topic. These are just examples to understand the right mechanics of their creation. <br /> <br /> EXAMPLE 1: (the idea is an effect similar to the oWoD for the Quietus discipline)<br /> Obfuscate 3 Auspex 3(???)<br /> <br /> It creates a silent area where people inside it can't hear any kind of sound. The area affected is equal to Blood Potency x 2 yards.<br /> <br /> Adding to the requisite Blood Potency could be that the effect area is an entire city (in order to mimic the hig power value of the discipline above 6)???<br /> <br /> EXAMPLE 2: <br /> Obfuscate 3 Celerity 5<br /> <br /> The vampire teleport itself behind an enemy making a surprise attack with a bonus on the dice pool equal to celerity and then disappear again. The only way the enemy has to hit the vampire is a chance roll. The vampire could use this power in a scene for a number of time equal to his Blood Potency and it can be used on the same target or on more target. <br /> Question: Could this power lead to multiple attack/use on the same turn (maybe just on different target)<br /> <br /> EXAMPLE 3:<br /> Vigor 5 Celerity 5<br /> <br /> The attack hit with strenght and speed. The vampire add the sum of vigor and celerity to the attack dice pool and lowers the defense of the target of the celerity value. The single active power of both the discipline can still be activated.<br /> <br /> EXAMPLE 4:<br /> Auspex 4 Vigor 1-2 (???)<br /> The vampire can give consistency to his mind power. He acquire telekinetic power with which he can move/trhow object with a dice pool equal to Intelligence(or wits) + Auspex, or even pull or lift enemies after win the contested roll based on: Wits+Auspex vs Resolve + Blood Potency (primal urge). After that he can consider the enemy like the object for the turn.<br /> <br /> EXAMPLE 5:<br /> Nightmare 5 Vigor (???)<br /> <br /> The vampire make real the wrost fear of the target. Spiders, Shadows monsters of every kind become physical and hunt or attack the target for the scenes. The victim can't act normally against these nightmares becouse his fear. The prefeared action should be to run away. If he is forced to fight his pool are lowered of Blood potency value of the vampire.<br /> <br /> What do you think about??<br /> Do you have any suggestions? Have I used the mechanichs of devotion properly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-12-2015, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T10:35:00-07:00","id":624467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions#post624000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EXAMPLE 1: (the idea is an effect similar to the oWoD for the Quietus discipline)<br /> Obfuscate 3 Auspex 3(???)<br /> <br /> It creates a silent area where people inside it can't hear any kind of sound. The area affected is equal to Blood Potency x 2 yards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how Auspex ties into this Devotion. Auspex is about supernaturally enhancing the user's perceptive abilities, this Devotion just negates sound. I think this could be done just with Obfuscate 2 and maybe Vigor 1. Maybe base the range on Vigor instead of Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions#post624000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding to the requisite Blood Potency could be that the effect area is an entire city (in order to mimic the hig power value of the discipline above 6)???</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, if you want to make this an Elder Devotion, maybe increase the Vigor requirement a bit, increase the Vitae cost by a lot, make the range city-wide, and add Dominate 3 so the people affected by it don't remember afterwords that everyone's hearing went out for a few minutes (so it's not a tremendous masquerade breach).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions#post624000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EXAMPLE 2: <br /> Obfuscate 3 Celerity 5<br /> <br /> The vampire teleport itself behind an enemy making a surprise attack with a bonus on the dice pool equal to celerity and then disappear again. The only way the enemy has to hit the vampire is a chance roll. The vampire could use this power in a scene for a number of time equal to his Blood Potency and it can be used on the same target or on more target. <br /> Question: Could this power lead to multiple attack/use on the same turn (maybe just on different target)</div> </div> </div> </div>Clerity 5 seems excessive here. Celerity already allows you to move so fast you appear to teleport, and lets you use that to make a surprise attack. You're basically adding Obfuscate to allow you to disappear after the attack. I'd drop the Celerity retirement to 2, make it cost 3 Vitae. Leave out the part about the chance roll to hit, just give them the normal -5 to hit a target they can't see. Between that and the user's Defense, most attackers should be on a chance die to hit anyway. Change the bonus to the attack roll to + Obfuscate instead of + Celerity (Obfuscate already does this). Limit the number of times it can be used per round by Celerity, not by Blood Potency (again, this is how Celerity already works.) And no, this shouldn't allow multiple attacks. It's already technically allowing multiple actions by letting you activate Obfuscate and make an attack in the same turn, let's not <i>totally</i> break the action economy here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions#post624000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EXAMPLE 3:<br /> Vigor 5 Celerity 5<br /> <br /> The attack hit with strenght and speed. The vampire add the sum of vigor and celerity to the attack dice pool and lowers the defense of the target of the celerity value. The single active power of both the discipline can still be activated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure what you're going for with this one. Just a straight +10 to hit? I guess it could work, seems a bit boring though. I think a more interesting Devotion for combining the strength of Vigor and the speed of Celerity would be one that allowed you to combine your dots in both for the active effects of either. For something like that I'd just require a dot in each and the Fighting Finesse Merit, and you could only use the Devotion on attacks using the Finessed specialty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions#post624000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EXAMPLE 4:<br /> Auspex 4 Vigor 1-2 (???)<br /> The vampire can give consistency to his mind power. He acquire telekinetic power with which he can move/trhow object with a dice pool equal to Intelligence(or wits) + Auspex, or even pull or lift enemies after win the contested roll based on: Wits+Auspex vs Resolve + Blood Potency (primal urge). After that he can consider the enemy like the object for the turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really like this one thematically because 2e Auspex isn't supposed to be psychic power, it's enhanced perception. But, I don't think there's really any other Discipline that would work better for a telekinesis Devotion. I would recommend putting the Vigor requirement at 1, and basing its effects off the Telekenesis Merit from GMC, but have it scale based on your dots in Vigor instead of your dots in the Merit, and make it cost Vitae instead of Willpower to activate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions#post624000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EXAMPLE 5:<br /> Nightmare 5 Vigor (???)<br /> <br /> The vampire make real the wrost fear of the target. Spiders, Shadows monsters of every kind become physical and hunt or attack the target for the scenes. The victim can't act normally against these nightmares becouse his fear. The prefeared action should be to run away. If he is forced to fight his pool are lowered of Blood potency value of the vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just make this a pure Nightmare Devotion, no need for Vigor. I'd also model it's effects on <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MepXf7K3F9mEENRp4O5suRph8w_GsSkK7PzTdwnEkmI/pub\" target=\"_blank\">the playtest version of Nightmare 5</a>, which already had rules for making the victim's hallucinations real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions#post624000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think about??<br /> Do you have any suggestions? Have I used the mechanichs of devotion properly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good ideas. I think your mechanics could use some streamlining, and gave my suggestions on how to do that. Also it seems like you're tending towards really high prerequisite dots for effects that you could probably achieve with lower for ratings. I get the feeling you're trying to create Elder Devotions like Juggernaut's Gait. If that's what you're going for, I think you can go even bigger with your effects. Most of these seem like pretty straightforward combinations of the things the component Disciplines already do (with the exception of the Telekenesis one). Part of the point of Devotions though is creating something greater than the sum of their parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T12:08:04-07:00","id":624539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions?p=624467#post624467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clerity 5 seems excessive here. Celerity already allows you to move so fast you appear to teleport, and lets you use that to make a surprise attack. You're basically adding Obfuscate to allow you to disappear after the attack. I'd drop the Celerity retirement to 2, make it cost 3 Vitae. Leave out the part about the chance roll to hit, just give them the normal -5 to hit a target they can't see. Between that and the user's Defense, most attackers should be on a chance die to hit anyway. Change the bonus to the attack roll to + Obfuscate instead of + Celerity (Obfuscate already does this). Limit the number of times it can be used per round by Celerity, not by Blood Potency (again, this is how Celerity already works.) And no, this shouldn't allow multiple attacks. It's already technically allowing multiple actions by letting you activate Obfuscate and make an attack in the same turn, let's not <i>totally</i> break the action economy here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought to use celerity as bonus to the attack pool cause the &quot;strenght&quot; is given by the mass (and we can't do anything to rise it if we don't reach a certain percentage of the light speed :P ) and the velocity of the hit. Obfuscation let you disappear or not.... While celerity give to the attack the velocity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions?p=624467#post624467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really like this one thematically because 2e Auspex isn't supposed to be psychic power, it's enhanced perception. But, I don't think there's really any other Discipline that would work better for a telekinesis Devotion. I would recommend putting the Vigor requirement at 1, and basing its effects off the Telekenesis Merit from GMC, but have it scale based on your dots in Vigor instead of your dots in the Merit, and make it cost Vitae instead of Willpower to activate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the last power of Auspex let the vampire leaves his body concretizing his....will?? Consciousnees??? I thought about it developing this devotion<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway thank you for the tips <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T12:50:23-07:00","id":624553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions?p=624539#post624539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought to use celerity as bonus to the attack pool cause the &amp;quot;strenght&amp;quot; is given by the mass (and we can't do anything to rise it if we don't reach a certain percentage of the light speed :P ) and the velocity of the hit. Obfuscation let you disappear or not.... While celerity give to the attack the velocity.</div> </div> </div> </div>But + Obfuscate to surprise attacks is something Obfuscate 3 already does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions?p=624539#post624539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the last power of Auspex let the vampire leaves his body concretizing his....will?? Consciousnees??? I thought about it developing this devotion</div> </div> </div> </div>Perception. It allows the vampire to project their perception outside of their body. But, like I said, I can't really think of any Discipline that would work better for a Telekenesis Devotion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions?p=624539#post624539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway thank you for the tips <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No problem, glad I could help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T15:57:41-07:00","id":624699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions#post624000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EXAMPLE 1: (the idea is an effect similar to the oWoD for the Quietus discipline)<br /> Obfuscate 3 Auspex 3(???)<br /> <br /> It creates a silent area where people inside it can't hear any kind of sound. The area affected is equal to Blood Potency x 2 yards.<br /> <br /> Adding to the requisite Blood Potency could be that the effect area is an entire city (in order to mimic the hig power value of the discipline above 6)???</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate 3, Celerity 1. What we're dealing with here is the same thing as Obfuscate, just without it being a mental effect. In actuality, its a bit weaker, all said and done, since Obfuscate hides the sight as well as sounds. Not sure why you want to blanket all sound in a city, though. Seems unnecessarily Masquerade-breachy for little benefit. Doable, but I'm at a loss to think -why- anyone would want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EXAMPLE 2:<br /> Obfuscate 3 Celerity 5<br /> <br /> The vampire teleport itself behind an enemy making a surprise attack with a bonus on the dice pool equal to celerity and then disappear again. The only way the enemy has to hit the vampire is a chance roll. The vampire could use this power in a scene for a number of time equal to his Blood Potency and it can be used on the same target or on more target. </div> </div> </div> Seems excessive. I mean, with Obtenebration, we have: <b>Iteru</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">With this gift, the Khaibit can travel rapidly through shadows. She dissolves into one part of the shadow, and emerges anywhere along the same patch of shade. This can be shadow created by the Tyet. Spend a Vitae reflexively, and the character fades into and out of the shadow instantly. If using this as part of a Dodge action, roll her Dodge with the rote quality once per scene.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Celerity 2</span></span></span><br /> <br /> What you're effectively doing with your devotion is just a hit-and-run using the usual Celerity, then disappearing. What you're effectively doing is remaking the Hair Trigger devotion, but a bit wordier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question: Could this power lead to multiple attack/use on the same turn (maybe just on different target) </div> </div> </div>Only if you're hitting different opponents, as per the rules for rapid fire. No multiple attacks on a single target. That's not a thing in 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EXAMPLE 3:<br /> Vigor 5 Celerity 5<br /> <br /> The attack hit with strenght and speed. The vampire add the sum of vigor and celerity to the attack dice pool and lowers the defense of the target of the celerity value. The single active power of both the discipline can still be activated. </div> </div> </div> I'm assuming that we're talking about spending a point of vitae here. What you're doing is adding +10 dice for a point of vitae. I'm not sure if a devotion is really the place for boosting Physical Augmentation like that. It feels like it should be a Coil thing. Plus, as an elder, you're already getting physical boosts from high BP (bonus in frenzy) plus more vitae to spend a turn. And I'm personally not sold with adding Vigor three times - once with the passive effect, once with active, and once with this. That's a lot. As it is now, the three physicals are roughly equal. This kinda just blows it away with a massive boost of power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EXAMPLE 4:<br /> Auspex 4 Vigor 1-2 (???)<br /> The vampire can give consistency to his mind power. He acquire telekinetic power with which he can move/trhow object with a dice pool equal to Intelligence(or wits) + Auspex, or even pull or lift enemies after win the contested roll based on: Wits+Auspex vs Resolve + Blood Potency (primal urge). After that he can consider the enemy like the object for the turn. </div> </div> </div> There's a coil that grants access to mortal supernatural merits, including telekinesis. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't really use Auspex for the base, though. Auspex is all about sensory powers, not forcing your will on the world. I think Dominate might be a better base, maybe? Or perhaps just all physical powers? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EXAMPLE 5:<br /> Nightmare 5 Vigor (???)<br /> <br /> The vampire make real the wrost fear of the target. Spiders, Shadows monsters of every kind become physical and hunt or attack the target for the scenes. The victim can't act normally against these nightmares becouse his fear. The prefeared action should be to run away. If he is forced to fight his pool are lowered of Blood potency value of the vampire. </div> </div> </div> This is what Nightmare does normally, but as hallucinations instead of physical objects. It should also be in Condition form, IMHO. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What do you think about??<br /> Do you have any suggestions? Have I used the mechanichs of devotion properly? </div> </div> </div> You have a lot of overlap with what powers can already do, just a with some variation in execution. That's a lot of effort for effectively tweaking powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T17:38:10-07:00","id":624803,"title":"","content":"Your example 1 seems to be a variation of Cloak the Gathering to me. Maybe you can add Vigor to increase the number of people affected, Vigor times 10 as a multiplier for instance. The problem with affecting a whole city is you just committed a Masquerade breach so massive vampires from all over the world are going to find you and ash you. At best, you should be limited to a location size that might be affected by a brown out. If you limit the devotion to Elders then I could see maybe blood potency in city blocks as a range and not worry about numbers for this limited effect. If I was to start from scratch, I would look at Majesty and Dominate instead of Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T01:17:08-07:00","id":625213,"title":"","content":"First of all, you could already think of costs, both in Vitae, WP and the like, and in XP. Keep in mind that the XP cost is usually equal to half the requisite dots, but it can be raised or lowed at your discretion to represent the real power of the Devotion.<br /> <br /> That thread, by the way, can serve the purpose of being an exercise to all of us, maybe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">EXAMPLE 1: (the idea is an effect similar to the oWoD for the Quietus discipline)<br /> Obfuscate 3 Auspex 3(???)<br /> <br /> It creates a silent area where people inside it can't hear any kind of sound. The area affected is equal to Blood Potency x 2 yards.<br /> <br /> Adding to the requisite Blood Potency could be that the effect area is an entire city (in order to mimic the hig power value of the discipline above 6)???</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally think a pure Obfuscate here would be better, at 3 since you're dealing with a variation of Cloak of Night. I hardly see the necessity for Vigor or Celerity in this effect. It would cost 1XP and have the effect of suppressing sound to everyone in a radius based on Obfuscate. I don't even think it should cost Vitae, since it's weird enough to not be that useful, and usually your own sound is already covered by Obfuscate. Making silence without Vitae cost would be precisely the purpose of this Devotion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">EXAMPLE 2: <br /> Obfuscate 3 Celerity 5<br /> <br /> The vampire teleport itself behind an enemy making a surprise attack with a bonus on the dice pool equal to celerity and then disappear again. The only way the enemy has to hit the vampire is a chance roll. The vampire could use this power in a scene for a number of time equal to his Blood Potency and it can be used on the same target or on more target. <br /> Question: Could this power lead to multiple attack/use on the same turn (maybe just on different target)</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets break it. You activate Celerity for speed, then reflexively activates Obfuscate, get a bonus for the Attack roll and hugely penalizes he attack of your target...<br /> <br /> <b>Charlaquin</b>, Obfuscate don't get added on the surprise attack roll, just let it happen.<br /> <br /> <b>MCN</b>, Iteru gives defensive bonuses, he wants an offensive Devotion, even if with a defensive aftereffect.<br /> <br /> This Devotion is actually giving a lot of bonuses. It lets you Obfuscate immediately upon doing an attack, a huge bonus by itself, and also making the attack proper more likely to hit. I would change a lot of things here.<br /> <br /> What about this: you move at a speed determined by your Celerity, but thanks to Obfuscate your target loses normal Defense against you (but not his own Celerity). You keep Obfuscate active immediately after the attack, but just for a turn. You can use this Devotion once per scene per dot of Obfuscate. It costs 3 Vitae to activate and 2 XP to acquire. Requisites: Obfuscate 3, Celerity 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">EXAMPLE 3:<br /> Vigor 5 Celerity 5<br /> <br /> The attack hit with strenght and speed. The vampire add the sum of vigor and celerity to the attack dice pool and lowers the defense of the target of the celerity value. The single active power of both the discipline can still be activated.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of giving an extra effect to Vigor + Celerity isn't a bad one, but this execution, as already stated by both <b>Charlaquin</b> and <b>MCN</b>, is both overpowered and boring. Think first about the idea, if it is a bullet-fist, or a full-body tackle after some running. Them think about the <u>minimum</u> power needed, not the maximum. 5s are for Juggernaut's Gait and the like. A basic new trick should be at 1s, a good but non-elder one at 3s, 2s being a middle term. 4 is mainly to round out some numbers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">EXAMPLE 4:<br /> Auspex 4 Vigor 1-2 (???)<br /> The vampire can give consistency to his mind power. He acquire telekinetic power with which he can move/trhow object with a dice pool equal to Intelligence(or wits) + Auspex, or even pull or lift enemies after win the contested roll based on: Wits+Auspex vs Resolve + Blood Potency (primal urge). After that he can consider the enemy like the object for the turn.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Charlaquin</b> said all I could, already. At maximum I would say that it either requires Vigor 1 and 1 XP or Vigor 2 and 2 XP, simply to keep it from scratch cheaper than Telekinesis itself (and so avoid it being worse than the Coil cited by <b>MCN</b>).<br /> <br /> My only addendum is that I actually like the requisite of Auspex 4. First, Auspex 5 don't let you extend just your perception, since Auspex 1 lets you perceive Auspex 5 as another vampire present, in the book's words. Second, Auspex 4 itself is the level where you link with another mind. And it DOES let you put thoughts in that other mind, so it is already your Beast reaching out. In fact, in all descriptions Auspex is THE Discipline about you Beast reaching out to the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">EXAMPLE 5:<br /> Nightmare 5 Vigor (???)<br /> <br /> The vampire make real the wrost fear of the target. Spiders, Shadows monsters of every kind become physical and hunt or attack the target for the scenes. The victim can't act normally against these nightmares becouse his fear. The prefeared action should be to run away. If he is forced to fight his pool are lowered of Blood potency value of the vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nightmare 5 already causes a good amount of damage, at 4 it can raise a better hallucination, at 2 can force the victim to flee and at 1 causes a greater potential number of hallucinations. So here you have to define a better goal for the effect. I can think easily of a Nightmare 1 or 2 effect combined with Vigor 1 to create illusions for bashing damage, or a Nightmare 5 with Vigor 3 to actually summon solid monsters from minds to the world of flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T02:04:26-07:00","id":625222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions?p=625213#post625213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That thread, by the way, can serve the purpose of being an exercise to all of us, maybe?<br /> <br /> This Devotion is actually giving a lot of bonuses. It lets you Obfuscate immediately upon doing an attack, a huge bonus by itself, and also making the attack proper more likely to hit. I would change a lot of things here.<br /> <br /> What about this: you move at a speed determined by your Celerity, but thanks to Obfuscate your target loses normal Defense against you (but not his own Celerity). You keep Obfuscate active immediately after the attack, but just for a turn. You can use this Devotion once per scene per dot of Obfuscate. It costs 3 Vitae to activate and 2 XP to acquire. Requisites: Obfuscate 3, Celerity 1.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thanks you all for your tips. Like Monteparnas said: these devotions wants to be just a training to understand the mechanics of their creations. For example about the first one: I know is worse then Obfuscate. I just wanted to understand what powers combine to achieve different effects. Is hard for me to decide the right prerequisites in order to achieve a specific effect, and is also hard to give to the devotions the right power effect.<br /> In this version of the devotion, after the attack I'd keep obfusctae active immediately....so the effect of the -5 penality to be hit remains?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions?p=625213#post625213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of giving an extra effect to Vigor + Celerity isn't a bad one, but this execution, as already stated by both <b>Charlaquin</b> and <b>MCN</b>, is both overpowered and boring. Think first about the idea, if it is a bullet-fist, or a full-body tackle after some running. Them think about the <u>minimum</u> power needed, not the maximum. 5s are for Juggernaut's Gait and the like. A basic new trick should be at 1s, a good but non-elder one at 3s, 2s being a middle term. 4 is mainly to round out some numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just in order to make an example (not for a real scenario), what should be the effect of a physical devotion like this one with a level of blood potency really hig? Like 7-8-9???<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions?p=625213#post625213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Charlaquin</b> said all I could, already. At maximum I would say that it either requires Vigor 1 and 1 XP or Vigor 2 and 2 XP, simply to keep it from scratch cheaper than Telekinesis itself (and so avoid it being worse than the Coil cited by <b>MCN</b>).<br /> <br /> My only addendum is that I actually like the requisite of Auspex 4. First, Auspex 5 don't let you extend just your perception, since Auspex 1 lets you perceive Auspex 5 as another vampire present, in the book's words. Second, Auspex 4 itself is the level where you link with another mind. And it DOES let you put thoughts in that other mind, so it is already your Beast reaching out. In fact, in all descriptions Auspex is THE Discipline about you Beast reaching out to the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I though about that. I like the idea of doors open or shut without touching it, or enemy pushed away or attached to the wall :P . Could a devotion like it let the user's to levitate? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T05:19:23-07:00","id":625315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thanks you all for your tips. Like Monteparnas said: these devotions wants to be just a training to understand the mechanics of their creations. For example about the first one: I know is worse then Obfuscate. I just wanted to understand what powers combine to achieve different effects. Is hard for me to decide the right prerequisites in order to achieve a specific effect, and is also hard to give to the devotions the right power effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a rule of thumb, the Devotion have to add something you can't achieve with the standard Disciplines, have a cost in XP that makes it interesting without making it better than them, and the requisites have the purpose of not making the Devotion a shortcut to power. The core idea is being a cheap variation of powers you already have. All of that can mean a lot of things, though.<br /> <br /> So a Devotion that creates an area of silence is of limited use, but it IS of some use, so it is a valid Devotion. Specially if, being worse than the main power, it is cheaper to activate. At 1 XP it is reasonable to take even if so limited, but the cost can increase if you later find that it can be abused in unexpected ways. With Obfuscate 3 (Cloak of Night) as prerequisite, you already have access to the standard &quot;invisibility&quot; power, and this Devotion is a partial &quot;invisibility&quot; (inaudibility to be precise), so you can't use the Devotion as a shortcut to pass non-detected before acquiring the main power. If it was something the main power couldn't do, it would be a good idea for it to cost at least 2 XP, or keep the cost in Vitae.<br /> <br /> Other good rule of thumb for the requisites is to make them at the lowest level in with a thematic similar effect is achieved. At the same time you use them to avoid shortcuts, you have to keep them at relatively low levels, for a Devotion is MEANT to be used with some ease, unless it is of humongous power, like Juggernaut's Gait, the ever-present example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this version of the devotion, after the attack I'd keep obfusctae active immediately....so the effect of the -5 penality to be hit remains?</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. The idea is to partially balance the effect with the Vitae cost. The Devotion is roughly equivalent to activate both Celerity and Cloak of Night, and with them you wouldn't have a too hard time achieving a similar effect anyway (depriving the target of Defense by surprise and disappearing for a -5 on his attack), but it cost 1 more Vitae to activate and neatly manages to do it all with way more ease. The cost of 2 XP means it isn't too cheap, but also not unfeasible. I have to add that I'm not sure about it being already balanced, but I believe it isn't too OP for the task.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just in order to make an example (not for a real scenario), what should be the effect of a physical devotion like this one with a level of blood potency really hig? Like 7-8-9???</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to say, but the core assumption is that the Devotion should always add something new. Maybe you could have an effect like old Masquerade high-level Potency Flicker, where you deliver a blow at short distance with minimal movement, or maybe a blow able to send the target several yards backwards and prone, or yet a running blow that can target several people at the same time.<br /> <br /> Remember, tough, that high level Devotions don't by default need other requisites than some Disciplines at 5. Again, our beloved Juggernaut's Gait: it makes you completely immune to any kind of damage, at a cost of 5 Vitae per turn. Its balance is good and built in its own rules: with Resilience 5, it is the ultimate stage of Resilience conceivable, its cost is actually lower than a new dot of Resilience since it isn't a constant help, and the cost in blood makes it naturally more powerful at higher BP, because it is almost futile before BP 5, but from them on your increasing pool of Vitae makes you able to hold it longer.<br /> <br /> Always keep the balance: do not let it be a shortcut to power, but also keep the requisites as low as possible. Internal costs are also part of the balance, and BP is an option, but one for when needed even to make Elder Devotions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes I though about that. I like the idea of doors open or shut without touching it, or enemy pushed away or attached to the wall :P . Could a devotion like it let the user's to levitate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, I can't see why not. The simplest way to do it, though, is really to look at the Telekinesis Merit. Not just because it already have the rules, but because it already IS a thing in the game, so you have to worry with balance against it. The Devotion is cheaper because it relies on you having a lot of requisites before and them turns Vigor into Telekinesis. But it shouldn't by itself at any moment be better than Telekinesis or subsume its rules.<br /> <br /> All said and done, I would also like to read some thoughts on my ideas about these Devotions while I can't bring some of my own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T06:13:33-07:00","id":625372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/624000-examples-of-devotions?p=625213#post625213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Charlaquin</b>, Obfuscate don't get added on the surprise attack roll, just let it happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>...yes, it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire: the Requiem Second Edition, page 138</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the vampire attacks someone or cries out, Cloak of Night continues to obscure him, adding Obfuscate to the surprise roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T07:20:04-07:00","id":625447,"title":"","content":"Yes it's written in vampire the requiem second edition but not in blood and smoke book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I didn't read before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T09:13:19-07:00","id":625591,"title":"","content":"Looking at it again though, I think it adds to the roll to surprise the opponent, not the attack roll. So we were both wrong <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now